{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/glib\/patternspecprotocol\/patternmatch(stringlength:string:stringreversed:)"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/PatternSpecProtocol"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/PatternSpecProtocol\/patternMatch(stringLength:string:stringReversed:)"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"Matches a string against a compiled pattern.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"GLib","externalID":"s:4GLib19PatternSpecProtocolPAAE12patternMatch12stringLength0G00G8ReversedSbSi_SPys4Int8VGSgAKtF","modules":[{"name":"GLib"}],"title":"patternMatch(stringLength:string:stringReversed:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"patternMatch","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"stringLength","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"string"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"UnsafePointer","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SP"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@gchar","text":"gchar"},{"kind":"text","text":">!, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"stringReversed"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UnsafePointer","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SP"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@gchar","text":"gchar"},{"kind":"text","text":">?) -> "},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"platforms":[],"role":"symbol"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"patternMatch"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"stringLength","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"string"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SP","text":"UnsafePointer","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@gchar","text":"gchar"},{"kind":"text","text":">!, "},{"text":"stringReversed","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SP","text":"UnsafePointer","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@T@gchar","text":"gchar"},{"text":">? = nil) -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Passing the correct"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"length of the string given is mandatory. The reversed string can be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"omitted by passing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NULL"},{"type":"text","text":", this is more efficient if the reversed"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"version of the string to be matched is not at hand, as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_pattern_match()"},{"text":" will only construct it if the compiled pattern","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"requires reverse matches.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Note that, if the user code will (possibly) match a string against a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"multitude of patterns containing wildcards, chances are high that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"some patterns will require a reversed string. In this case, it’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"more efficient to provide the reversed string to avoid multiple"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"constructions thereof in the various calls to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g_pattern_match()"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Note also that the reverse of a UTF-8 encoded string can in general"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"not be obtained by [func","type":"text"},{"code":"GLib.strreverse","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"]. This works only if the string"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"does not contain any multibyte characters. GLib offers the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[func","type":"text"},{"code":"GLib.utf8_strreverse","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] function to reverse UTF-8 encoded strings.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"pattern_match is deprecated:"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"Use [method@GLib.PatternSpec.match] instead"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/PatternSpecProtocol":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/PatternSpecProtocol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/glib\/patternspecprotocol","title":"PatternSpecProtocol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PatternSpecProtocol","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PatternSpecProtocol"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"code":"GPatternSpec","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" struct is the ‘compiled’ form of a glob-style pattern.","type":"text"}]},"doc://GLib/documentation/GLib/PatternSpecProtocol/patternMatch(stringLength:string:stringReversed:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Matches